```python
#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""N0 draft: flat-space spherical scalar-wave convergence and invariant harness.

Scope (proposed, unassigned): node N0 "Flat-space scalar-wave test" in the
numerics group, provisionally class-bound to AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH.

Fixed Minkowski background. Massless, real scalar field, spherical symmetry.
No self-gravity, no black-hole formation, no critical-collapse or cosmic-
censorship claim. Convergence order and invariant diagnostics only.

Equation: u_tt = u_rr + (2/r) u_r, u=u(t,r), r in (0,R]
Reduced variable: v = r*u  ->  v_tt = v_rr, v(t,0)=0, v(t,R)=0 (standing box)
Exact standing-wave solution with k = m*pi/R:
    v_exact(t,r) = sin(k r) cos(k t) / k
    u_exact(t,r) = sin(k r) cos(k t) / (k r)
Energy (conserved by the PDE): H = 1/2 ∫ (v_t^2 + v_r^2) dr
Identity: H = E_u/(4π), E_u = 4π * 1/2 ∫ (u_t^2 + u_r^2) r^2 dr
"""
```

